[projlang/design] Design with the user: projection language semantics (reviewing)
Projection-language semantic decisions recorded; concrete selector and value syntax deferred to grammar and schema work.
-> core/freeze
> 2026-07-21: Select defines a layer's structure; it may generate elements, take references to existing elements, or both.
> 2026-07-21: A generated select element is an ordinary definition: it supplies everything required of any other element definition at its layer definition site.
> 2026-07-21: Generated select definitions obey the same reference rules as every other definition; no separate recursion or stratification semantics are required.
> 2026-07-21: Invert takes a group of elements and reverses the direction sign of every connection in it.
> 2026-07-21: Decorate is one global finalization phase after all structural select and invert evaluation. Decorations cannot feed structural evaluation. Checks operate only over decorations, are lossy only in their own result, and do not discard finalized data.
> 2026-07-21: Structural folding joins references by address under the one-definition rule. Decoration identity and constraints belong to extension namespaces and schemas; generated-selector and symbolic-value syntax are deferred until a concrete example requires them.
@artifact text/markdown ./proposals/projection-language.md
---
[schemas/shapes] Design with the user: shapes schema (reviewing)
Artifact: proposals/shape-schema.md.
Define shape values as coarse layout plus ordered dimensions, where each dimension is a positive literal or a first-class axis reference. Keep topology and token correspondence explicit; do not infer spatial meaning from names or media type.
-> extension-namespaces/minting
-> schemas/axes
-> schemas/meta
> 2026-08-26: Shape values use layout enum(scalar,vector,sequence,grid,volume) plus ordered literal-or-axis-reference dimensions.
> 2026-08-26: TiTok's latent is represented as a sequence and V-JEPA 2 frame features as a grid; layout does not infer spatial correspondence.
> 2026-08-26: Shape compatibility is a narrow later check over explicit ports, not a new core graph primitive or implicit shape inference.
@artifact text/markdown ./proposals/shape-schema.md
@guidance text/markdown ./spec/grimoire.md
---
[schemas/axes] Design with the user: axes schema (reviewing)
Artifact: proposals/axes-schema.md.
Define symbolic axis values as name plus optional description. Use first-class address references and normal locality; fixed extents remain shape values. The initial fixture anchors declarations on dimension-owning ports.
-> extension-namespaces/minting
-> schemas/meta
> 2026-08-26: Axis values are product{name:text, description:optional(text)}; names are labels and do not imply time, height, width, batch, token, or feature semantics.
> 2026-08-26: Fixed extents belong to shapes, not axis declarations, so one symbolic axis can support multiple model variants and cuts.
> 2026-08-26: The first anchoring fixture places an axis declaration on a dimension-owning port; broader group anchoring remains an explicit gap.
