[schemas/meta] Design with the user: schema definition format (reviewing)
The format schemas themselves are written in: versioned and machine-checkable.
-> core/freeze
> 2026-07-21: The schema body is a closed Grimoire-native algebra. Its constructors, constraints, and validation behavior are specified by this format; it does not delegate arbitrary schema-body semantics to external dialects or extension keywords.
> 2026-07-21: The closed initial algebra has scalar refinement, labeled product, homogeneous sequence, tagged alternative, first-class address reference, and explicit absent | present(T). A schema declares its allowed element kinds. Initial scalar refinements are finite scalar kind, positive integer, finite number, text, and closed enumeration.
> 2026-07-21: The format provides the necessary bootstrap productions to describe and validate its own closed algebra. Bootstrap uses the same constructors and does not invoke a second schema language.
@artifact text/markdown ./proposals/schema-format.md
