[execution/boundary] Specify static execution boundary (reviewing)
Artifact: proposals/execution-boundary.md.
Define the static account for streaming, recurrent, and closed-loop systems. Execution regime is finalized metadata; structural state, causal, and action paths remain ordinary connections; runtime clocks, buffers, rollouts, controllers, and replanning remain external. Missing runtime-facing producers in a cut are visibly unresolvable.
-> architecture/vocabulary
> 2026-08-26: Execution values use regimes static, streaming, recurrent, and closed-loop, with optional horizon and rate plus required external-consumer status.
> 2026-08-26: Execution values never create feedback or causal paths; those paths are structural only when the described model interface contains them.
> 2026-08-26: Runtime observation, buffering, state progression, action execution, sampling, and replanning remain outside pure projection evaluation.
> 2026-08-26: A missing runtime-facing producer in a cut is reported as an unresolvable dependent layer, not silently treated as empty or open-loop.
